id: pm-62n4kk
title: "GH-828: init status registries must expose one coherent alias contract"
description: "Fresh trackers embed status aliases in settings.json and write schema/statuses.json, but the two generated registries disagree specifically on the in_progress alias."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:init","area:schema",github-intake,integrity
created_at: "2026-07-30T11:28:54.704Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T11:28:54.704Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Fresh init emits faithful alias data or an explicitly uniform summary; regeneration remains deterministic; fixtures cover in_progress and canceled aliases across both files; documentation states the authoritative registry
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make generated status registry projections visibly coherent and non-authoritative caches explicit
value: Reviewers and agents do not infer drift or hand-edit audited settings from contradictory generated data
impact: Eliminates systematic fresh-tracker schema review noise
parent: pm-doxj
